# ComposeIO Bus Storage — SMD Conversion, NOT YET RECONCILED [SPEC:CXC-BUSSTORE]

> ⛔ **NOTHING IN THIS FILE HAS BEEN CHECKED AGAINST THE IMPLEMENTATION.** Every claim below was
> carried across from prose. None has been ruled CURRENT, BEHIND or AHEAD of the code by this
> document, and no reader should cite it as though one had. `lifecycle-position` says the same thing
> in a form a query can read: **`converted — gap-analysis PENDING`**.
>
> This is **pass 1 of the ratified two-step**. Migration confers authority
> (`[DEC-MIGRATE-SPEC-01-GATED-ON-GAP-ANALYSIS]`) — a `.lts` node is queryable, citable, and treated
> as current by every downstream reader, so converting stale prose does not carry staleness forward,
> it **LAUNDERS** it: prose nobody trusted becomes a node everyone cites. The banner and the
> lifecycle property are what stop that here. **Pass 2 is `factlattice-gap-analyzer`**, which reads
> `.lts` only — so this conversion is what makes the analysis possible at all, and the verdict is
> deliberately left to it rather than taken by the author who wrote these nodes.
>
> The gap this closes is real: `bus_storage` is a product this project builds, deploys and depends
> on at every boot, and the corpus named it **55 times — every one a CONSUMER declaring a
> dependency** — while describing it not once. Its registry entry is a 129-token stub; its BROWSER
> carries 327. The viewer for the thing was specified and the thing was not.
>
> `[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED]` — see [CXC-BUSSTORE-PLACEMENT].

