## 4. The asset namespace

### [CXC-BUSSTORE-ASSET-NS] The path is hierarchical, and the sources name no convention for it

- what-the-source-says: §7.3 states the asset path is hierarchical and gives `album_art/current.jpg`. DP-CIO-23 gives the same shape in a `bus://` reference. That is the whole of the specification.
- naming-conventions: EMPTY. No source names a required or recommended prefix, reserved directory, or path grammar. Nothing states which paths a device or widget is expected to find.
- registry-of-assets: EMPTY. No source describes a manifest, index or schema of asset paths, nor any validation that a published path is one a consumer will look for.
- case-sensitivity: EMPTY. No source states whether asset paths are case-sensitive.
- who-may-write: EMPTY. No source states which actors are expected to PUT assets or under what prefixes.
- why-this-matters: the boot sequences in section 5 depend on a device and a publisher agreeing on an exact path. The sources describe both halves and never state the contract between them, which makes this an unusually load-bearing EMPTY.
- source-section: spec/01-composeio-bus-protocol.smd §7.3; spec/00-composeio-design-principles.smd DP-CIO-23
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-BUSSTORE]

